Phase 1 — Reconnaissance and endpoint discovery

Identify API specifications, routes, HTTP methods, parameters, content types, authentication requirements, and exposed documentation.

Phase 2 — Authentication and authorization

Validate login, sessions, tokens, role enforcement, tenant isolation, BOLA/IDOR, and function-level authorization.

Phase 3 — Input and business-logic testing

Test validation, parameter tampering, injection classes, mass assignment, and inconsistent server-side controls.

Phase 4 — File and network attack surfaces

Assess uploads, downloads, path traversal, SSRF protections, archive extraction, and file access controls.

Phase 5 — Resilience and configuration

Review rate limits, security headers, CORS, TLS, error handling, exposed debug features, and API versioning.

Phase 6 — Evidence and reporting

Reproduce suspected vulnerabilities, confirm impact, preserve sanitized request/response evidence, and retest fixes.
